course: dictionary
lesson: 9695
title: Sugary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sugary comes from sugar, so it often tells you that something contains a lot of sugar. «Water and milk are the best drinks; juice is very sugary, so have only a small glass once a day.» The words water, milk and small glass are clues: sugary means full of sugar, so juice is a drink to have only sometimes.
explain: Sugary can also describe a smile, voice or film that is too sweet and seems false. «The actor gave a sugary smile, but it did not look real.» The word but is the clue. The smile looks sweet on the outside, yet it does not seem honest.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Put in «full of sugar» for sugary in the juice sentence and it still makes sense. Try «too sweet and not real» in the smile sentence and it also fits, so you know which meaning the author chose.
fact: Sugary means containing a lot of sugar, or tasting very sweet.
fact: Sugary can also mean too sweet or sentimental in a way that seems false, like «a sugary film».
fact: Sugary foods and drinks give quick energy, but eaten often they can cause tooth decay and weight problems.
fact: Bacteria in your mouth feed on sugar and make acid that damages tooth enamel, so brushing twice a day helps.
fact: Food labels show how much sugar is in a product, so check them when you shop.
exercise: «Sugary cereals with cartoon characters are put on low shelves.» What does sugary mean here? | *Containing a lot of sugar | Very cold | Shiny and bright | Made of sand
exercise: «Her sugary smile did not look real, and the film was far too sweet.» What does sugary suggest? | Full of sugar to eat | Cold and wet | Loud and angry | *Too sweet in a way that seems false
exercise: Which of these is a sugary treat? | Carrot sticks | Water | Plain milk | *A sweet, iced cake
test: «It was reported that some governments taxed sugary drinks to help people drink less sugar.» What are the sugary drinks in this sentence? | Drinks that are very hot | *Drinks with a lot of sugar in them | Drinks made from water only | Drinks sold only in glass bottles
test: Which is the best way to protect your teeth from sugary food? | Keep sweets in your mouth overnight | *Brush your teeth twice a day | Drink only juice at every meal | Eat sugary snacks all day long
exam: Jayden says sugary only means tasting sweet. «The villain's sugary voice hid a nasty trick.» What does sugary mean in this sentence? | Full of sugar to eat | Loud and angry | Very cold and quiet | *Too sweet in a way that seems false
